        "DETAILED EXPLANATION — Leadership helps people coordinate toward shared outcomes. Communication requires both explaining ideas and listening carefully. Effective teamwork makes expectations explicit, invites concerns and uses feedback to improve the work rather than attack people. Connect this explanation to “Communicate clearly”: ask what the concept helps you understand or decide, what information it depends on and how the outcome might change if an important condition changed. Define unfamiliar terms and add a small example so that understanding goes beyond memorising words.",
        "KEY TERMS — Objective: intended result; delegation: assigning responsibility; active listening: listening to understand; feedback: specific information for improvement; conflict: disagreement over needs, ideas or resources. Build a glossary in your own notes. For each term, write a definition in your own words, an example and one related term it could be confused with. This helps you decide when a concept is appropriate and when it is not.",
