        "COMMON ERRORS AND QUALITY CHECKS — Unclear ownership, assuming silence means agreement, personal blame and ignoring quieter contributors. Check accuracy, relevance, safety, completeness and clarity before relying on your result. Inspect source information and calculations where relevant, respect privacy and applicable rules, and state uncertainties. Safety-critical work must use approved procedures and appropriately qualified supervision.",
        "PRACTICAL EXERCISE — Write a team briefing with goal, roles, deadline, update method and a respectful way to raise concerns. Record your goal, resources, steps, result, difficulty and one improvement for a second attempt. Use fictional or anonymised data whenever real names, customer records or private account details are unnecessary.",
