      "LESSON-SPECIFIC THINKING — Ask what you should be able to explain or do after studying Active recall and spaced practice. Write an answer, demonstrate it with an example, check it against reliable information and identify what additional practice would help you work independently. Go deeper by asking why the approach fits, what alternative you considered and what new evidence could change your answer. Explain your reasoning to a classmate who has not studied the lesson.",
