          "LEARNING OUTCOMES — By the end of this lesson in Data Analysis & Spreadsheet Skills, you should be able to explain the topic in your own words, recognise when it is useful, apply it to a realistic task and check whether the result is reliable. You should also be able to describe one limitation instead of assuming that one method works in every situation.",
          "DETAILED EXPLANATION — Data analysis turns organised observations into information for a defined question. Rows store records and columns store fields; formulas calculate values, summaries reveal patterns and charts communicate comparisons. Reliable conclusions depend on data quality and transparent methods. Connect this explanation to “Introduction and Key Concepts”: ask what the concept helps you understand or decide, what information it depends on and how the outcome might change if an important condition changed. Define unfamiliar terms and add a small example so that understanding goes beyond memorising words.",
