          "DETAILED EXPLANATION — Research uses a transparent method to answer a focused question. Critical thinking evaluates the quality and relevance of information, considers alternative explanations and distinguishes what evidence supports from what remains uncertain. Connect this explanation to “Introduction and Key Concepts”: ask what the concept helps you understand or decide, what information it depends on and how the outcome might change if an important condition changed. Define unfamiliar terms and add a small example so that understanding goes beyond memorising words.",
